  <result aggregation-status="0" type="9">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Other indicators (P) and narrative explanation</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Please provide a short narrative explanation of the data here. (max 250 words)</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline year="2024"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-12-31"></period-end>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">We are pleased to submit the final report for the TA project. This project has been key in advancing our mission to provide safe drinking water to schools in Uganda, while offering lessons on the role of impact measurement. Through the development and implementation of the IMM system, we gathered critical data from 375 schools to better understand our beneficiaries. This data revealed that we are currently serving 209,376 children daily with safe drinking water. Additionally, the installation of 375 meters has enabled precise tracking of water usage and system performance, ensuring our solutions remain aligned with the needs of schools. Our business currently serves an average of 160 paying customers per month, (during the school terms), and we are operating at a cost recovery percentage of 100%. This means our revenues and operational costs are nearly equal, putting us at breakeven.The project also provided an opportunity to explore carbon credit financing as a potential avenue to enhance our impact. This exploration has sparked significant interest, and although there is still a lot to learn about carbon credit financing, we aim to advance carbon credit certification in the coming year, we will keep Aqua for All informed of the progress. Overall, this journey has been a learning experience, teaching us the importance of aligning business practices with measurable social impact, and we are grateful for Aqua for All&#xfffd;s support in this endeavor.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
